WEBVTT

00:00.300 --> 00:02.815
This is Click, the Python library behind

00:02.815 --> 00:05.330
thousands of command-line tools, open in VS

00:05.330 --> 00:07.844
Code with Deslop installed. Deslop has already

00:07.844 --> 00:10.359
read every Python file in the library

00:10.359 --> 00:12.874
and ranked the duplicate code it found.

00:12.874 --> 00:15.389
The worst copies sit at the top

00:15.389 --> 00:17.904
of this list, and the warning under

00:17.904 --> 00:20.419
this method says it exists more than

00:20.419 --> 00:20.778
once.

00:21.578 --> 00:24.324
Near the top, Deslop pairs two exception

00:24.324 --> 00:27.071
classes: No Such Option and No Such

00:27.071 --> 00:29.817
Command. Compare puts them side by side.

00:29.817 --> 00:32.563
The constructor, the default message and the

00:32.563 --> 00:35.310
close-match suggestions are the same code. The

00:35.310 --> 00:38.056
only change is that option became command,

00:38.056 --> 00:39.625
all the way through.

00:40.425 --> 00:43.039
This finding is exact. The Bash, Z

00:43.039 --> 00:45.652
shell and PowerShell completion classes each define

00:45.652 --> 00:48.266
the same get completion args method, line

00:48.266 --> 00:50.879
for line. I follow each file link

00:50.879 --> 00:53.493
to read the copies in place before

00:53.493 --> 00:54.613
I change anything.

00:55.413 --> 00:57.856
The other two classes can reuse the

00:57.856 --> 01:00.299
Bash method directly, so I replace both

01:00.299 --> 01:02.742
copies with one line each and save.

01:02.742 --> 01:05.185
Deslop scans again straight away and the

01:05.185 --> 01:07.628
finding is gone. Then I run the

01:07.628 --> 01:10.072
shell completion tests from Click, and all

01:10.072 --> 01:11.468
fifty eight still pass.
